      "c_angela"
     ],
     "cc": [],
     "subject": null,
     "body": "I'd advise against it: OFM's instructions ask for costs we can support, and an unexplained 20% is exactly what they cut first, along with our credibility on the rest. A stronger approach is to state the assumptions they could challenge (an April start, the 33.5% benefits rate) and show the dropout data. If you want room, we could request the January start as an option ($237,600) with the April case ($118,800) as the base. Your call.",
     "attachments": [],
     "meta": {}
    }
   ]
