     "subject": "Re: DOL apprenticeship grant budget",
     "body": "Fixed the rate to 16.9%, thanks! On the $12,000 advisory meetings line: four quarterly meetings, 30 people, lunch at each, plus room rental. Is lunch OK to keep?",
     "attachments": [],
     "meta": {}
    },
    {
     "id": "t4-mara.w2",
     "at": "D4 13:50",
     "author": "worker",
     "to": [
      "c_fednick"
     ],
     "cc": [],
     "subject": null,
     "body": "Keep it, but justify it: under 2 CFR 200.432, meals at a meeting are allowable when they're necessary to carry out the meeting (e.g., a full-day working session where breaking for lunch isn't practical) and reasonable. Put the agenda length, the per-person cost (use the state lunch rate) and why lunch is needed in the narrative, and keep room rental separate. If the meetings are two hours, I'd drop the lunch.",
     "attachments": [],
     "meta": {}
    }
